<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kingdom of Ma'in</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Minaean Kingdom, Minaeans</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kingdom of Ma'in was an ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-arabia">South Arabian</a> state of the Minaeans in the Jawf valley of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a>, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qarnawu">Qarnaw</a> and a religious centre at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baraqish">Yathill</a> (Baraqish). Flourishing roughly from the sixth or fourth century to the first century BCE, it controlled much of the caravan trade in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/incense">incense</a>, and Minaean merchants left inscriptions at Dedan in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delos">Delos</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-main.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Ma'in" width="320" height="329" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Wario2 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kingdom_of_Ma%27in.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
